## Command Description
The main functionality of this command is to search and locate a specific text pattern throughout a a certain number of lines within a file, which also results in the printing and showcasing of these word pattern findings in the terminal. 
The primary way how to run this code is to type node, along with the name of the js server, a keyword or pattern that you want to search for, the name of the file in which you're searching through and the maximum number of lines that you want to search. Example: node ff.js error server.log 10
This specific code combines the functionality and utility of the GREP function, which is used to allow for a user to search keywords or patterns throughout a file, along with the HEAD function which is used to display the lines in which the keyword is found in.

